    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q1-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A certain type of drug takes on average 8 minutes to act. a) Assuming this time is Normally distributed with a standard deviation of 1.5, ( ) find the time under which the drug begins to act in 5% of the patients. 4 A patient is given this drug. b) Given that the drug took less than 8 minutes to act, determine the probability that it actually took more than 5 minutes to act. ( ) 4 c) Given instead that the drug took more than 5 minutes to act, determine the probability that it actually took less than 8 minutes to act. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Redrawing two graphs:\" style=\"--madas-width:524.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Let X ∼N(8, 1.52). (a) The fifth percentile is 8 + 1.5Φ−1(0.05) ≈5.53 min . [M1] Choose the lower five-percent quantile [A1] find its standard score [A1] rescale using 1.5 and 8 [A1] evaluate in minutes\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q1-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"(b) The standard score at 5 is (5 −8)/1.5 = −2. Between 5 and 8 the probability is Φ(0) −Φ(−2) = 0.5 −0.02275 . . . . Both conditional questions have this same numerator: Here P(X &lt; 5) = Φ(−2) [B1] and P(X &lt; 8) = 0.5. [A1] The conditional probability is (0.5 −Φ(−2))/0.5 ≈0.9545 . [M1] [A1] (c) With X &gt; 5 as the conditioning event, the probability is (0.5 −Φ(−2))/(1 −Φ(−2)) ≈0.4884 . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
