    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-t/q5",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The probability distribution of a discrete random variable X is given by  k x = 1  1 P ( X = x ) =  P ( X = x − 1 ) x = 2,3,4 2  0 otherwise  where k is a positive constant. Three independent observations of X are made, denoted by X , X and X , and the 1 2 3 variable Y is defined as Y = X + X + X . 1 2 3 ( ) If  Y is an even number, determine the probability that  Y is greater than 9. 10\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q5-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:568.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The probability weights for 1, 2, 3, 4 are k, k/2, k/4, k/8. [M1] The normalising equation is k(1 + 1/2 + 1/4 + 1/8) = 1, hence 15k/8 = 1, k = 8/15. Their sum is 1, so the probabilities are 8/15, 4/15, 2/15, 1/15. [A1] One X is even with probability 1/3. [A1] For an even sum, one or three observations are even: [A1] Thus P(Y even) = 3(1/3)(2/3)2 + (1/3)3 [M1] [A1] = 13/27. The even sums above 9 are 10 and 12. [A1] Sum 10 arises from permutations of (2, 4, 4) and (3, 3, 4), with total probability 24/153. [A1] In units of 1/153, the first pattern contributes 3(4)(1)(1) = 12, and the second 3(2)(2)(1) = 12. The factor 3 places the unequal score: Sum 12 arises from (4, 4, 4), with probability 1/153. [A1] The requested probability is 25/153 1 13/27 = 65 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The probability distribution of a discrete random variable X is given by  k x = 1  1 P ( X = x ) =  P ( X = x − 1 ) x = 2,3,4 2  0 otherwise  where k is a positive constant. Three independent observations of X are made, denoted by X , X and X , and the 1 2 3 variable Y is defined as Y = X + X + X . 1 2 3 ( ) If  Y is an even number, determine the probability that  Y is greater than 9. 10 "
