      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"On a common denominator the sum is (k2 + 2k + 4)/(k2 + 2k). The positive excess is 4/(k2 + 2k). Mutually exclusive events would have a union with probability equal to that sum, which is impossible: [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
