    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Relative to a fixed origin O , the horizontal unit vectors i and j are pointing due east and due north, respectively. Two particles are moving with constant acceleration on a horizontal surface where O is contained. At time t = 0 s , one of the particles is at the point with position vector ( 7 i + 2 j m , ) ms− and constant acceleration ( 1 1 ms−. moving with velocity ( + ) 1 − ) 2 i 2 j i j 4 2 At time t = 0 s , the other particle is at the point with position vector ( i − j m , ) ms− and constant acceleration ( 1 1 1 ) ms−. 2 moving with velocity ( 2 i − 2 j ) i − j 2 4\" style=\"--madas-width:560.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q8-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Calculate the distance between the two particles, at the instant when they are moving in parallel directions to one another. ( ) [You may ignore any motion taking place prior to time t = 0 s ] 11\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-t/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The velocities at time t are (1 + t/4, 2 −t/2) and (2 + t/2, −2 −t/4) in component form: [B1] [A1] The second east component is twice the first, which is positive for t ≥0. [M1] [A1] Parallel motion therefore requires −2 −t/4 = 2(2 −t/2), [M1] [A1] giving t = 8. [A1] Clearing denominators gives −8 −t = 16 −4t, hence 3t = 24. The relative position then has components 23 −33 = −10 and 2 −(−25) = 27. At that instant r = r0 + 8u + 32a [A1] gives positions (23, 2) and (33, −25) in metres: [A1] Their separation is √ q (−10)2 + 272 = 829 m ≈28.8 m . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 8 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
